You are writing the bullet points for a tailored resume. Be ruthless about ATS keyword matching and STAR format.

Return ONLY a JSON object with this exact schema:
{
  "headline": string,                            // one line under the candidate's name
  "summary": string,                             // 2-3 sentences max
  "skills": [string, ...],                       // 8-15 keyword-rich skills, JD must-haves first
  "experience": [
    {
      "company": string,                         // EXACTLY as in master resume
      "title": string,                           // EXACTLY as in master resume
      "start": string,                           // EXACTLY as in master resume (YYYY-MM)
      "end": string | null,                      // EXACTLY as in master resume
      "bullets": [
        {
          "text": string,                        // the actual bullet shown on resume
          "source": "experience",
          "source_ref": "experience:<company>:<start>",
          "star": {"s": "...", "t": "...", "a": "...", "r": "..."},
          "keywords_hit": [string, ...],         // JD keywords this bullet covers
          "has_estimate": boolean                 // true if "r" contains a metric you ESTIMATED
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "project_bullets": [
    {
      "text": string,
      "source": "project",
      "source_ref": "project:<project_id>",
      "star": {"s": "...", "t": "...", "a": "...", "r": "..."},
      "keywords_hit": [string, ...],
      "has_estimate": boolean
    }
  ],
  "cover_paragraph": string                      // 4-6 sentences, ready to paste in cover letter field
}

HARD RULES (validate.py will reject violators):
- NEVER change company names, titles, or dates from the master resume.
- At most 3 `bullets` per experience entry and 2 `project_bullets` per selected project (quality over quantity).
- Keep each STAR sub-field (`s`, `t`, `a`, `r`) to one short sentence so the JSON fits in one response.
- Each `bullets` entry must trace to an experience the user actually has.
- Each `project_bullets` entry must reference one of the SELECTED project ids.
- If you ESTIMATE a metric (the user didn't supply it), set has_estimate=true and put "[ESTIMATE]" inside the result clause.
- STAR format: every bullet's "text" field must imply Situation, Task, Action, Result. Action verbs in past tense.
- Cover keywords from must_have_keywords first, then nice_to_have_keywords. Aim for >=70% must-have coverage.
- COMPACT OUTPUT (required for local models): at most 2 bullets per experience entry; at most 2
  project_bullets total; set "star" to {} on every bullet; keep each bullet text under 180 chars.
- Escape double quotes inside strings as \". Output JSON only. No prose, no code fences.

